  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>morse.decode</keyword>
  <short_description>Decode International Morse code into text.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>text = morse.decode(code)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>text = morse.decode(code, name, value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[text, unknown] = morse.decode(code, ...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>code</param_name>
      <param_description>a character row vector or scalar string; dot/dash groups separated by spaces, words separated by '/' (or, when no '/' is present, by two or more spaces).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>name, value</param_name>
      <param_description>optional name-value pairs: 'Dot' (default '.'), 'Dash' (default '-'), 'OnUnknown' ('mark' (default) or 'error'), 'Placeholder' (default '?').</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>text</param_name>
      <param_description>a character row vector, upper case (the form Morse preserves).</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>unknown</param_name>
      <param_description>a cellstr of the unique dot/dash groups that matched no character.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Inverse of <b>morse.encode</b>. It round-trips any text made only of characters in the table. An unrecognized dot/dash group is replaced by 'Placeholder' ('mark') or raises <b>morse:unknownCode</b> ('error').</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography>ITU-R Recommendation M.1677-1, International Morse code.</bibliography>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[morse.decode('... --- ...')
morse.decode(morse.encode('HELLO WORLD'))]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
